<div id="2026-09-12-inventory-order-flow" class="cl-entry">
<h3>2026-09-12 — Group "Order by supplier" from Stock Levels + non-orderable exclusions</h3>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>What.</strong> Stock Levels (low-only) now has a category filter and a "🛒 Order selected by supplier" action. Tick rows (or leave none to order all) → one draft PO per supplier is created. BOM parents expand recursively to their short leaf components (BOMs-within-BOMs), so ticking a kit orders its parts. Cost centres (overhead/cost), 3D-printed parts, and capital equipment/printers are flagged non-orderable and excluded from the orderable count and dashboard.</p>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>Why.</strong> User needed to group-order restock (esp. filaments) and not see printers/depreciation/printed parts in the buy list. Verified against live API: orderable low/missing for site 3d = 10 (hardware + 1 PETG), down from 96 once overhead/printed/equipment excluded.</p>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>Files.</strong> <code>Util/Inventory/Purchasing.pm</code> (new <code>orderable_low_list</code> — exclusion + recursive BOM expansion + supplier grouping), <code>Controller/Inventory.pm</code> (stock_levels category filter + is_orderable flag; new <code>po_order_group</code>), <code>Controller/Accounting.pm</code> (dashboard low_stock exclusions), <code>root/Inventory/stock/levels.tt</code> (category dropdown, checkboxes, order button + JS).</p>
</div>
